---
/* Match a syllabus to the site, on the teacher's own computer.

   A teacher pastes a syllabus (or opens a text or Word file) and picks the class's level. The page
   lists the syllabus's own topics in the syllabus's own order, each with the lessons and films
   that teach it at that level, a simpler one for review and a deeper one for stretch, and says
   plainly where the site has nothing yet. The teacher unticks what they will not use, then copies
   the list or prints it.

   Nothing pasted is sent anywhere: the matching is src/lib/syllabus-match.mjs running in the
   browser over static files, and no model is asked. That has to hold with scripts off, blocked or
   not yet loaded too, so there is no <form> here and the box has no name: nothing on this page can
   submit the text. The buttons are switched on by the script. This page loads no analytics script,
   so no third-party code runs where a syllabus is typed. No account is needed.

   "Add ticked lessons to a class" is written but OFF (ADD_TO_CLASS in src/lib/teach-match.ts)
   until it has been tried on a real class. /teach/syllabus/ is a different tool (it sends the
   syllabus to an AI model and needs a teacher account); the link to it below is OFF as well. */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../../styles/teach.css';
import '../../../styles/hop.css';
import '../../../styles/teach-match.css';
import { LEVEL_LABEL, LEVEL_KEYS } from '../../../lib/hop-words.mjs';

/* OFF: whether to link the AI planner (/teach/syllabus/) from this page. Turning it on is the
   site owner's call, since that tool spends his model budget. */
const SHOW_AI_PLANNER_LINK = false;
const sample = `Week 1: Lab safety, scientific method
Week 2: Cell theory & microscopes
Week 3: Cell membrane, diffusion and osmosis
Week 4: Photosynthesis
Week 5: Cellular respiration; Unit 1 Test
Week 6: Mitosis and meiosis
Week 7: Heredity - Punnett squares
Week 8: Thanksgiving break`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Match my syllabus to lessons — STEMhop" description="Paste your syllabus and pick your class's level. For each topic you get the lessons and films that teach it, a simpler one for review and a deeper one for stretch. It runs on your computer; nothing is sent." noAnalytics>
  <article class="wrap tc tm" data-tm>
    <p class="tc-eyebrow tm-noprint"><a href="/teachers/">Resources for teachers</a> · Match my syllabus</p>
    <h1>Match your syllabus to lessons</h1>
    <p class="tc-lede tm-noprint">Paste it and pick your class's level. You get your topics, in your order, with the lessons and films that teach each one.</p>

    <div class="tm-form tm-noprint" data-tm-form>
      <label class="tm-label" for="tm-text">Your syllabus <span>the schedule of topics is enough</span></label>
      <textarea id="tm-text" rows="8" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" placeholder={sample}></textarea>
      <div class="tm-row tm-go">
        <label class="tm-level">Your class's level
          <select data-tm-level autocomplete="off">
            {LEVEL_KEYS.map((k, i) => <option value={i} selected={k === 'high-school'}>{LEVEL_LABEL[i]}</option>)}
          </select>
        </label>
        <button class="tc-btn" type="button" data-tm-go disabled>Match my syllabus</button>
      </div>
      <div class="tm-row tm-more">
        <label class="tm-file">Or open a syllabus file
          <input type="file" data-tm-file aria-describedby="tm-file-hint" disabled accept=".txt,.md,.csv,.docx,text/plain,text/markdown,text/csv,application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document" />
        </label>
        <button class="tc-btn ghost" type="button" data-tm-sample disabled>Try a sample</button>
      </div>
      <p class="tm-hint" id="tm-file-hint">Plain text or Word (.docx). For a PDF, open it, copy the schedule and paste it in the box.</p>
      <p class="tc-error" data-tm-file-err role="alert"></p>
      <p class="tm-private"><strong>Your syllabus stays on this computer.</strong> The matching runs in your browser. What you paste or open is never sent, no AI reads it, and you need no account.</p>
    </div>
    <noscript><p class="tc-note">This page needs JavaScript, because the matching runs in your browser, so the buttons do nothing without it. The lessons are mapped to the Virginia standards for <a href="/teachers/life-science/">grade 7 Life Science</a> and <a href="/teachers/biology/">high school Biology</a>, and <a href="/courses/">every course</a> lists its lessons in order.</p></noscript>

    <p class="tm-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-tm-status></p>
    <section class="tm-result" data-tm-result hidden>
      <h2 tabindex="-1" data-tm-h>Your syllabus, matched</h2>
      <p class="tm-sum" data-tm-sum></p>
      <p class="tm-sum tm-noprint" data-tm-elsewhere hidden></p>
      <div class="tm-tools tm-noprint">
        <button class="tc-btn ghost" type="button" data-tm-copy>Copy the list</button>
        <button class="tc-btn ghost" type="button" data-tm-print>Print</button>
        <button class="tc-btn ghost" type="button" data-tm-assign hidden>Add ticked lessons to a class</button>
        <span class="tc-ok" data-tm-msg role="status"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="tm-assign tm-noprint" data-tm-assign-box role="status" tabindex="-1" hidden></div>
      <ol class="tm-rows" data-tm-rows></ol>
      <details class="tm-skipped tm-noprint" data-tm-skipped hidden><summary></summary><ul></ul></details>
      <p class="tm-foot">The matching is done by rules, not by a person: it compares your words with each idea's names and with lesson titles, and it leaves a topic unmatched when it is not sure. Which lessons teach each idea was written by AI models from the lessons and checked by a second one. A person has not yet read every one. <a href="/contact/">Tell me</a> when a match is wrong.</p>
      {SHOW_AI_PLANNER_LINK && <p class="tm-foot tm-noprint">Have a teacher account? <a href="/teach/syllabus/">The AI planner</a> also picks simulations and flashcards and saves a list your students can open. It sends your syllabus to an AI model.</p>}
    </section>
  </article>

  <script is:inline type="application/json" data-tm-sample-text set:html={JSON.stringify(sample)}></script>
  <script>
    import { start } from '../../../lib/teach-match';
    start();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
